AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	15590	17470	.	-	0	ID=cds-CCP42736.1;Parent=gene-Rv0014c;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv0014c,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP42736,GOA:P9WI81,InterPro:IPR000719,InterPro:IPR002290,InterPro:IPR005543,InterPro:IPR008271,InterPro:IPR011009,InterPro:IPR017441,PDB:1MRU,PDB:1O6Y,PDB:2FUM,PDB:2KUD,PDB:2KUE,PDB:2KUF,PDB:2KUI,PDB:3F61,PDB:3F69,NCBI_GP:CCP42736.1;Name=CCP42736.1;Note=Rv0014c%2C (MTCY10H4.14c)%2C len: 626 aa. PknB%2Ctransmembrane serine/threonine-protein kinase (see citations below). Contains PS00107 Protein kinases ATP-binding region signature%2C and PS00108 Serine/Threonine protein kinases active-site signature. Contains Hank's kinase subdomain. Belongs to the Ser/Thr family of protein kinases. Experimental studies show evidence of auto-phosphorylation on serine/threonine residues. PknB has been shown to be a substrate for PstP and its kinase activity is affected by PstP-mediated dephosphorylation. PknB and PstP (Rv0018c) may act as a functional pair in vivo to control mycobacterial cell growth.;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=pknB;inference=protein motif:PROSITE:PS00108;locus_tag=Rv0014c;product=Transmembrane serine/threonine-protein kinase B PknB (protein kinase B) (STPK B);protein_id=CCP42736.1;transl_table=11
