AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	874732	876390	.	+	0	ID=cds-CCP43529.1;Parent=gene-Rv0782;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv0782,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP43529,GOA:P71834,InterPro:IPR001375,InterPro:IPR002470,InterPro:IPR023302,InterPro:IPR029058,UniProtKB/TrEMBL:P71834,NCBI_GP:CCP43529.1;Name=CCP43529.1;Note=Rv0782%2C (MTCY369.26)%2C len: 552 aa. Probable ptrBb%2Csecond part of protease II%2C equivalent to C-terminus of NP_302455.1|NC_002677 protease II from Mycobacterium leprae (724 aa). Also highly similar to N-termini of many proteases II e.g. P24555|PTRB_ECOLI|TLP|B1845 protease II from Escherichia coli strains K12 and HB101 (707 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 1251%2C E(): 0%2C (42.7%25 identity in 489 aa overlap)%3B etc. ORFs Rv0782 and Rv0781 appear to be a frameshifted homologues of protease II%2C but we can find no error in the cosmid sequence to account for this. Belongs to peptidase family S9A%3B also known as the prolyl oligopeptidase family. Note that previously known as ptrBa. Conserved in M. tuberculosis%2C M. leprae%2C M. bovis and M. avium paratuberculosis%3B predicted to be essential for in vivo survival and pathogenicity (See Ribeiro-Guimaraes and Pessolani%2C 2007).;gbkey=CDS;gene=ptrBb;locus_tag=Rv0782;product=Probable protease II PtrBb [second part] (oligopeptidase B);protein_id=CCP43529.1;transl_table=11
