AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	1034903	1036015	.	+	0	ID=cds-CCP43676.1;Parent=gene-Rv0928;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv0928,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP43676,GOA:P9WGT7,InterPro:IPR005673,InterPro:IPR024370,NCBI_GP:CCP43676.1;Name=CCP43676.1;Note=Rv0928%2C (MTCY21C12.22)%2C len: 370 aa. PstS3 (previously known as phoS2)%2C phosphate-binding lipoprotein component of inorganic phosphate transport system (see citations below)%2C highly similar to others from Mycobacterium leprae e.g. Q50099|PSTS3|PHOS1 phosphate-binding protein 3 precursor (328 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 1772%2C E(): 0%2C (79.6%25 identity in 328 aa overlap)%3B and highly similar to others e.g. AAF74819.1|AF137360_1|AF137360 periplasmic phosphate permease from Mycobacterium avium (369 aa). Also highly similar to Rv0932c|MTCY08D9.07|pstS2 phosphate-binding periplasmic lipoprotein (370 aa)%3B and Rv0934|pstS1 phosphate-binding periplasmic lipoprotein (374 aa) from Mycobacterium tuberculosis (Mycobacterium tuberculosis seems to have three PstS-like proteins%2C others being Rv0932c and Rv0934c). Contains lipoprotein signature (PS00013) at N-terminus. Belongs to family of phosphate receptors for bacterial ABC-type lipoprotein transporters.;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=pstS3;inference=protein motif:PROSITE:PS00013;locus_tag=Rv0928;product=Periplasmic phosphate-binding lipoprotein PstS3 (PBP-3) (PstS3) (PHOS1);protein_id=CCP43676.1;transl_table=11
