AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	1037920	1039914	.	-	0	ID=cds-CCP43679.1;Parent=gene-Rv0931c;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv0931c,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP43679,GOA:P9WI79,InterPro:IPR000719,InterPro:IPR001258,InterPro:IPR008271,InterPro:IPR011009,InterPro:IPR011042,InterPro:IPR013017,InterPro:IPR017441,PDB:1RWI,PDB:1RWL,NCBI_GP:CCP43679.1;Name=CCP43679.1;Note=Rv0931c%2C (MTCY08D9.08)%2C len: 664 aa. PknD (alternate gene name: mbk)%2C transmembrane serine/threonine protein kinase (see citations below)%2C equivalent to CAB62227.1|AJ250200 putative serine/threonine protein kinase from Mycobacterium bovis BCG (291 aa)%3B and highly similar in N-terminus to P54744|PKNB_MYCLE probable serine/threonine-specific protein kinase from Mycobacterium leprae (622 aa). Also highly similar to others%2Cparticularly in N-terminal half e.g. NP_243370.1|NC_002570 serine/threonine protein kinase from Bacillus halodurans (664 aa)%3B NP_268044.1|NC_002662 serine/threonine protein kinase from Lactococcus lactis (627 aa)%3B etc. Also highly similar to other serine/threonine protein kinases from Mycobacterium tuberculosis e.g. pknH (626 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 1398%2C E: 0%2C (49.3%25 identity in 540 aa overlap)%3B pknE (566 aa)%3B pknB (626 aa)%3B Rv3524 (343 aa)%3B etc. Contains Hank's kinase subdomain. Contains two transmembrane segments%2C which flank a highly repetitive region%2C suggesting a receptor-like anchoring. Belongs to the Ser/Thr family of protein kinases. Experimental studies show evidence of auto-phosphorylation on a serine residue. Appears to be co-transcribed with Rv0932c|pstS2.;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=pknD;inference=protein motif:PROSITE:PS00108;locus_tag=Rv0931c;product=Transmembrane serine/threonine-protein kinase D PknD (protein kinase D) (STPK D);protein_id=CCP43679.1;transl_table=11
