AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	1039936	1041048	.	-	0	ID=cds-CCP43680.1;Parent=gene-Rv0932c;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv0932c,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP43680,GOA:P9WGT9,InterPro:IPR005673,InterPro:IPR006059,NCBI_GP:CCP43680.1;Name=CCP43680.1;Note=Rv0932c%2C (MTCY08D9.07)%2C len: 370 aa. PstS2%2Cphosphate-binding lipoprotein component of inorganic phosphate transport system (see citations below)%2C highly similar to AAF74819.1|AF137360_1|AF137360 periplasmic phosphate permease from Mycobacterium avium (369 aa)%3B Rv0928|MTCY21C12.22|pstS3 phosphate-binding periplasmic lipoprotein from Mycobacterium tuberculosis (370 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 1601%2C E(): 0%2C (64.5%25 identity in 372 aa overlap)%3B and Rv0934|MTCY08D9.05c|pstS1 phosphate-binding periplasmic lipoprotein from Mycobacterium tuberculosis (374 aa) (Mycobacterium tuberculosis seems to have three PstS-like proteins%2C others being Rv0928 and Rv0934c). Also highly similar to MTCY08D9.05c|P15712|PAB_MYCTU protein antigen B precursor from Mycobacterium tuberculosis (374 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 460%2C E(): 2.7e-20%2C (31.2%25 identity in 375 aa overlap). Contains prokaryotic membrane lipoprotein lipid attachment site (PS00013) at N-terminus so the leader peptide of 22 aa is probably removed. Belongs to family of phosphate receptors for bacterial ABC-type lipoprotein transporters. Appears to be co-transcribed with Rv0931c|pknD|mbk.;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=pstS2;inference=protein motif:PROSITE:PS00013;locus_tag=Rv0932c;product=Periplasmic phosphate-binding lipoprotein PstS2 (PBP-2) (PstS2);protein_id=CCP43680.1;transl_table=11
