AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	1041264	1042094	.	+	0	ID=cds-CCP43681.1;Parent=gene-Rv0933;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv0933,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP43681,GOA:P9WQK9,InterPro:IPR003439,InterPro:IPR003593,InterPro:IPR005670,InterPro:IPR015850,InterPro:IPR017871,InterPro:IPR027417,NCBI_GP:CCP43681.1;Name=CCP43681.1;Note=Rv0933%2C (MTCY08D9.06c)%2C len: 276 aa. PstB%2Cphosphate-transport ATP-binding protein ABC transporter (see citations below)%2C thermostable ATPase%2C highly similar to others e.g. NP_348334.1|NC_003030 ATPase component of ABC-type phosphate transport system from Clostridium acetobutylicum (249 aa)%3B NP_212352.1|NC_001318 phosphate ABC transporter ATP-binding protein (pstB) from Borrelia burgdorferi (260 aa)%3B NP_390375.1|NC_000964 phosphate ABC transporter (ATP-binding protein) from Bacillus subtilis (269 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 762%2C E(): 0%2C (47.7%25 identity in 243 aa overlap)%3B etc. Also similar to other M. tuberculosis ABC transporters e.g. MTCY253.24%2C E(): 2.5e-15 and MTCY359.14c%2C E(): 3.4e-15. Contains PS00211 ABC transporters family signature%2C and PS00017 ATP/GTP-binding site motif A (P-loop). Belongs to the ATP-binding transport protein family (ABC transporters). Magnesium or calcium seem to have no influence on the functionality of this enzyme.;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=pstB;inference=protein motif:PROSITE:PS00211;locus_tag=Rv0933;product=Phosphate-transport ATP-binding protein ABC transporter PstB;protein_id=CCP43681.1;transl_table=11
