AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	2153889	2156111	.	-	0	ID=cds-CCP44675.1;Parent=gene-Rv1908c;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv1908c,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP44675,GOA:P9WIE5,InterPro:IPR000763,InterPro:IPR002016,InterPro:IPR010255,InterPro:IPR019793,InterPro:IPR019794,PDB:1SFZ,PDB:1SJ2,PDB:2CCA,PDB:2CCD,PDB:4C50,PDB:4C51,NCBI_GP:CCP44675.1;Name=CCP44675.1;Note=Rv1908c%2C (MTCY180.10)%2C len: 740 aa. KatG%2Ccatalase-peroxidase-peroxynitritase T (see citations below)%2C HPI. FASTA results: Q57215 catalase-peroxidase from Mycobacterium tuberculosis (740 aa) opt: 5081%2C E(): 0%2C(100%25 identity in 740 aa overlap). Contains peroxidases active site signature (PS00436) and ATP/GTP-binding site motif A (P-loop%3B PS00017). Cosmid sequence was corrected to agree with a sequencing read from the H37Rv genome. Deletions or defects in KATG gene cause isoniazid (INH) resistance. Belongs to the peroxidase family. Bacterial peroxidase/catalase subfamily. KATG transcription seems to be regulated by FURA|Rv1909c product. The catalase-peroxidase activity is associated with the amino-terminal domain but no definite function has been assigned to the carboxy-terminal domain. Predicted possible vaccine candidate (See Zvi et al.%2C 2008).;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=katG;inference=protein motif:PROSITE:PS00436;locus_tag=Rv1908c;product=Catalase-peroxidase-peroxynitritase T KatG;protein_id=CCP44675.1;transl_table=11
