AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	2161566	2162762	.	+	0	ID=cds-CCP44683.1;Parent=gene-Rv1916;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv1916,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP44683,GOA:O07717,InterPro:IPR006254,InterPro:IPR015813,UniProtKB/TrEMBL:O07717,NCBI_GP:CCP44683.1;Name=CCP44683.1;Note=Rv1916%2C (MTCY180.02c)%2C len: 398 aa. Probable aceAb%2Cisocitrate lyase (see citations below). Highly similar to the C-terminus of ACEA_MYCLE|P46831 isocitrate lyase from Mycobacterium leprae (606 aa)%2C FASTA results: opt: 1635%2CE(): 0%2C (86.3%25 identity in 278 aa overlap). Although this ORF and the upstream ORF representing the N-terminal half of aceA could be joined by a frameshift no error is apparent in the cosmid%2C or in a seqencing read from the genome of H37Rv. As this ORF has a RBS and transcriptional start immediately following the stop of the upstream ORF%2Cit is possible that they are expressed as two separate modules. In Mycobacterium tuberculosis strain CDC1551%2C aceA exists as a single gene%2C MT1966: the corresponding protein has been purified experimentally and seems have an active isocitrate lyase activity (see Honer et al.%2C 1999). For Mycobacterium tuberculosis strain H37Rv%2C immunoblot assay didn't detect AceAa or AceAb products (see Honer et al.%2C1999) but mRNA of AceAa|Rv1915 has been detected (see Betts et al.%2C 2002)%3B so AceAb|Rv1916 could be a pseudogene. Icl2 has 2-methyl-isocitrate lyase (MCL) activity in M. tuberculosis Erdman (See Munoz-Elias et al.%2C 2006).;gbkey=CDS;gene=aceAb;locus_tag=Rv1916;product=Probable isocitrate lyase AceAb [second part] (isocitrase) (isocitratase) (Icl);protein_id=CCP44683.1;transl_table=11
