AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	2201719	2202096	.	+	0	ID=cds-CCP44723.1;Parent=gene-Rv1955;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv1955,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP44723,GOA:P9WJA5,InterPro:IPR009241,NCBI_GP:CCP44723.1;Name=CCP44723.1;Note=Rv1955%2C (MTCY09F9.09c)%2C len: 125 aa. Possible higB%2Ctoxin%2C part of toxin-antitoxin (TA) operon with Rv1956 (See Pandey and Gerdes%2C 2005%3B Gupta%2C 2009). Start overlaps another ORF%2C Rv1954c (MTCY09F9.10). Start changed since first submission (-45 aa). Predicted to be an outer membrane protein (See Song et al.%2C 2008). Upon expression in E. coli has been shown to function as an antitoxin against Rv1956 (PubMed: 19016878)%3B It is not clear if these conflicting results are due to expression in a heterologous system%3B In various publications%2C both gene names higA and higB have been assigned to both Rv1955 and Rv1956%3B we have chosen to call Rv1955 higB after consulting the authors.;gbkey=CDS;gene=higB;locus_tag=Rv1955;product=Possible toxin HigB;protein_id=CCP44723.1;transl_table=11
