AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	2202138	2202587	.	+	0	ID=cds-CCP44724.1;Parent=gene-Rv1956;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv1956,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP44724,GOA:P9WJA7,InterPro:IPR001387,InterPro:IPR010982,NCBI_GP:CCP44724.1;Name=CCP44724.1;Note=Rv1956%2C (MTCY09F9.08c)%2C len: 149 aa. Possible higA%2Cantitoxin%2C part of toxin-antitoxin (TA) operon with Rv1955 (See Pandey and Gerdes%2C 2005%3B Gupta%2C 2009). Possible transcriptional regulatory protein%2C contains probable helix-turn-helix motif at aa 52-73 (+4.78 SD). Upon expression in E.coli Rv1956 has been shown to function as a toxin inhibiting cell growth and colony formation that is neutralized by coexpression with Rv1955 (PubMed: 19016878)%3B It is not clear if these conflicting results are due to expression in a heterologous system. The gene names higA and higB have been assigned to both Rv1955 and Rv1956%3B we have chosen to call Rv1956 higA after consulting the authors.;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=higA;locus_tag=Rv1956;product=Possible antitoxin HigA;protein_id=CCP44724.1;transl_table=11
