AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	2943376	2943603	.	+	0	ID=cds-CCP45412.1;Parent=gene-Rv2614A;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv2614A,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP45412,UniProtKB/TrEMBL:Q79FC4,NCBI_GP:CCP45412.1;Name=CCP45412.1;Note=Rv2614A%2C len: 75 aa. Conserved hypothetical protein. The region from aa 10-35 is similar to part of C-terminal part of several triosephosphate isomerases e.g. P46711|TPIS_MYCLE|TPIA|TPI|ML0572|B1496_C1_127 from Mycobacterium leprae (261 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 112%2C E(): 0.95%2C (60.0%25 identity in 25 aa overlap)%3B and O08408|TPIS_MYCTU|TPIA|TPI|Rv1438|MT1482|MTCY493.16c from Mycobacterium tuberculosis (261 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 104%2C E(): 3.3%2C (60.0%25 identity in 25 aa overlap)%3B P19583|TPIS_CORGL|TPIA|TPI from Corynebacterium glutamicum (Brevibacterium flavum) (259 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 100%2CE(): 6%2C (45.45%25 identity in 33 aa overlap)%3B etc. Triosephosphate isomerases play an important role in several metabolic pathways (catalytic activity: D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate %3D dihydroxy-acetone phosphate). Nucleotide position 2943411 in the genome sequence has been corrected%2C T:C resulting in L12L.;gbkey=CDS;locus_tag=Rv2614A;product=Conserved hypothetical protein;protein_id=CCP45412.1;transl_table=11
