AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	3120566	3121552	.	-	0	ID=cds-CCP45614.1;Parent=gene-Rv2814c;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv2814c,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP45614,GOA:P9WKH9,InterPro:IPR001584,InterPro:IPR012337,InterPro:IPR025948,NCBI_GP:CCP45614.1;Name=CCP45614.1;Note=Rv2814c%2C (MTCY16B7.29)%2C len: 328 aa. Probable transposase subunit for IS6110. Identical to many other M. tuberculosis IS6110 transposase subunits. The transposase described here may be made by a frame shifting mechanism during translation that fuses Rv2814c and Rv2815c%2C the sequence UUUUAAAG (directly upstream of Rv2814c) maybe responsible for such a frameshifting event (see McAdam et al.%2C 1990). Start changed since first submission (+ 16 aa). This region is a possible MT-complex-specific genomic island (See Becq et al.%2C 2007).;end_range=3121552,.;gbkey=CDS;locus_tag=Rv2814c;partial=true;product=Probable transposase;protein_id=CCP45614.1;transl_table=11
