AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	3180548	3181762	.	-	0	ID=cds-CCP45671.1;Parent=gene-Rv2869c;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv2869c,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP45671,GOA:P9WHS3,InterPro:IPR001478,InterPro:IPR008915,NCBI_GP:CCP45671.1;Name=CCP45671.1;Note=Rv2869c%2C (MTV003.15c)%2C len: 404 aa. Rip%2Cmetalloprotease%2C regulates intramembrane proteolysis and controls membrane composition (rip%2C see Makinoshima and Glickman%2C 2005). Similar to site two protease (S2P) in higher eukaryotes. Conserved transmembrane protein%2Cequivalent to Q9CBU4|ML1582 probable integral membrane protein from Mycobacterium leprae (404 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 2250%2C E(): 1.1e-128%2C (82.2%25 identity in 404 aa overlap). Also weakly similar to other membrane proteins or hypothetical proteins e.g. Q9A710|CC1916 putative membrane-associated zinc metalloprotease from Caulobacter crescentus (398 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 368%2C E(): 7.8e-15%2C(28.1%25 identity in 427 aa overlap). Conserved in M. tuberculosis%2C M. leprae%2C M. bovis and M. avium paratuberculosis%3B predicted to be essential for in vivo survival and pathogenicity (See Ribeiro-Guimaraes and Pessolani%2C 2007). Cleaves PbpB|Rv2163c in a Zn2+ -dependent manner (See Mukherjee et al.%2C 2009). Cleaves proteins RskA|Rv0444c%2C RslA|Rv0736%2C and Rv3912%2C in M. tuberculosis Erdman (See Sklar et al.%2C 2010).;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=rip;locus_tag=Rv2869c;product=Membrane bound metalloprotease;protein_id=CCP45671.1;transl_table=11
