AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	3188008	3188871	.	-	0	ID=cds-CCP45679.1;Parent=gene-Rv2877c;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv2877c,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP45679,GOA:I6YEL8,InterPro:IPR003834,UniProtKB/TrEMBL:I6YEL8,NCBI_GP:CCP45679.1;Name=CCP45679.1;Note=Rv2877c%2C (MTCY274.08c)%2C len: 287 aa. Probable conserved integral membrane protein%2C Mer family possibly involved in transport of mercury%2C similar to others%2C and to the fourth protein of the mercury resistance operon of Streptomyces sp (or other organisms)%2C and to putative cytochrome-c biogenesis proteins e.g. Q9XBD1|CZA382.20C putative integral membrane transporter from Amycolatopsis orientalis (298 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 913%2C E(): 7.6e-46%2C(51.55%25 identity in 293 aa overlap)%3B P30344|MER4_STRLI mercury resistance probable HG transport protein from Streptomyces lividans (319 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 427%2CE(): 1.2e-17%2C (32.85%25 identity in 289 aa overlap)%3B Q9M5P3 putative cytochrome C biogenesis protein precursor from Arabidopsis thaliana (Mouse-ear cress) (354 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 229%2C E(): 4e-06%2C (29.85%25 identity in 221 aa overlap)%3B etc. Contains PS00044 Bacterial regulatory proteins%2C lysR family signature. Note that previously known as merT.;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;inference=protein motif:PROSITE:PS00044;locus_tag=Rv2877c;product=Probable conserved integral membrane protein;protein_id=CCP45679.1;transl_table=11
