AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	3805621	3807573	.	+	0	ID=cds-CCP46212.1;Parent=gene-Rv3391;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv3391,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP46212,GOA:O50417,InterPro:IPR002198,InterPro:IPR002347,InterPro:IPR013120,InterPro:IPR016040,UniProtKB/TrEMBL:O50417,NCBI_GP:CCP46212.1;Name=CCP46212.1;Note=Rv3391%2C (MTV004.49)%2C len: 650 aa. Possible acrA1%2Cmulti functional protein with fatty acyl-CoA reductase activity in C-terminal part. Indeed C-terminal part highly similar to P94129|ACR1 fatty acyl-CoA reductase from Acinetobacter calcoaceticus (295 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 767%2C E(): 1.4e-36%2C (45.4%25 identity in 260 aa overlap)%3B and similar to other oxidoreductases dehydrogenases/reductases e.g. Q9Y3A1 CGI-93 protein (similarity with SDR family) from Homo sapiens (Human) (291 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 363%2CE(): 1.5e-13%2C (38.65%25 identity in 194 aa overlap)%3B Q9L146|SC6D11.09 putative oxidoreductase (similarity with SDR family) from Streptomyces coelicolor (343 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 346%2C E(): 1.6e-12%2C (30.4%25 identity in 283 aa overlap)%3B Q9HSR4|YUSZ1|VNG0115G oxidoreductase from Halobacterium sp. strain NRC-1 (260 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 338%2C E(): 3.7e-12%2C (33.85%25 identity in 248 aa overlap)%3B etc. C-terminus also similar to Mycobacterium tuberculosis proteins Q10783|YF43_MYCTU|Rv1543|MTCY48.22c putative oxidoreductase (341 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 787%2C E(): 1.2e-37%2C (39.8%25 identity in 319 aa overlap)%3B O06413|Rv0547c|MTCY25D10.26c hypothetical 31.8 KDA protein (294 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 565%2C E(): 4.7e-25%2C (36.8%25 identity in 242 aa overlap)%3B O53398|Rv1050|MTV017.03 oxidoreductase (SDR family) (301 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 436%2C E(): 1.1e-17%2C (32.2%25 identity in 292 aa overlap). N-terminus (aa 1-320) is similar to P37693|HETM_ANASP polyketide synthase hetM from Anabaena sp. (506 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 188%2C E(): 1.3e-07%2C (27.7%25 identity in 361 aa overlap)%3B so certainly a multi-domain enzyme. Seems to belong to the short-chain dehydrogenases/reductases (SDR) family. Note that this ORF corresponds to the gene ORF2|Q11197 (see Yuan et al.%2C 1995)%2C but longer 266 aa%2C due to use of a more upstream start site.;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=acrA1;locus_tag=Rv3391;product=Possible multi-functional enzyme with acyl-CoA-reductase activity AcrA1;protein_id=CCP46212.1;transl_table=11
