AL123456.3	EMBL	CDS	4363417	4364757	.	-	0	ID=cds-CCP46712.1;Parent=gene-Rv3883c;Dbxref=EnsemblGenomes-Gn:Rv3883c,EnsemblGenomes-Tr:CCP46712,GOA:O05461,InterPro:IPR000209,InterPro:IPR015500,InterPro:IPR023834,UniProtKB/TrEMBL:O05461,NCBI_GP:CCP46712.1;Name=CCP46712.1;Note=Rv3883c%2C (MTCY15F10.29)%2C len: 446 aa. MycP1%2Cmembrane-anchored serine protease (mycosin) (see citations below)%2C equivalent to O33076|ML0041|MLCB628.04 probable secreted protease from Mycobacterium leprae (446 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 2448%2C E(): 1.5e-124%2C (79.15%25 identity in 446 aa overlap)%3B and highly similar%2C but in part%2C to several putative proteases from Mycobacterium leprae%3B Q9CBV3|ML1538 (567 aa) FASTA scores: opt: 902%2C E(): 3e-41%2C (37.25%25 identity in 556 aa overlap)%3B and Q9CD36|ML2528 (475 aa)%2CFASTA scores: opt: 873%2C E(): 9.4e-40%2C (42.7%25 identity in 459 aa overlap). Shows also similarity with several proteases from other organisms e.g. Q9PCD0|XF1851 serine protease from Xylella fastidiosa (1000 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 281%2C E(): 1.3e-07%2C (27.95%25 identity in 422 aa overlap)%3B P42780|BPRX_BACNO extracellular subtilisin-like protease precursor from Bacteroides nodosus (Dichelobacter nodosus) (595 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 270%2C E(): 3.2e-07%2C(28.9%25 identity in 384 aa overlap)%3B Q46541|APRV5 acidic protease V5 from Bacteroides nodosus (Dichelobacter nodosus) (595 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 264%2C E(): 6.8e-07%2C(28.65%25 identity in 384 aa overlap)%3B etc. Also highly similar to various proteins from Mycobacterium tuberculosis e.g. O53695|Rv0291|MTV035.19 probable membrane-anchored mycosin MYCP3 (461 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 1168%2C E(): 1.2e-55%2C (44.6%25 identity in 453 aa overlap)%3B O53945|Rv1796|MTV049.18 probable membrane-anchored mycosin MYCP5 (585 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 928%2C E(): 1.2e-42%2C(37.85%25 identity in 555 aa overlap) (note gap from aa 155-264)%3B and downstream ORF O05458|Rv3886c|MTCY15F10.26 probable membrane-anchored mycosin MYCP2 (550 aa)%2C FASTA scores: opt: 910%2C E(): 1.1e-41%2C (40.15%25 identity in 533 aa overlap) (note partial gap from aa 146-234)%3B etc. Equivalent to AAK48366 from Mycobacterium tuberculosis strain CDC1551 (411 aa) but longer 35 aa. Has signal sequence with possible signal peptidase I cleavage site in residues 19-21 (ASA) and hydrophobic stretch at C-terminus%2Cfollowed by short positively charged segment%2C that seems to act as a membrane anchor. Activated by Ca2+ (see Dave et al.%2C 2002). Contains three serine protease%2C subtilase family active site motifs: a aspartic acid active site motif (PS00136)%3B a histidine active site motif (PS00137)%3B and a serine active site motif (PS00138). Belongs to peptidase family S8 (also known as the subtilase family)%2Cpyrolysin subfamily. Conserved in M. tuberculosis%2C M. leprae%2C M. bovis and M. avium paratuberculosis%3B predicted to be essential for in vivo survival and pathogenicity (See Ribeiro-Guimaraes and Pessolani%2C 2007).;experiment=EXISTENCE: identified in proteomics study;gbkey=CDS;gene=mycP1;locus_tag=Rv3883c;product=Membrane-anchored mycosin MycP1 (serine protease) (subtilisin-like protease) (subtilase-like) (mycosin-1);protein_id=CCP46712.1;transl_table=11
